# No lazy deferral: shekyl-core's part

Estate rule [`22-no-lazy-deferral`](22-no-lazy-deferral.mdc) holds in every Shekyl repository.
This rule holds the part of it that only shekyl-core has: what a
FOLLOWUPS `Owner:` may resolve to here, and the gate that holds it.

## The `Owner:` cell

In shekyl-core a FOLLOWUPS row's **`Owner:`** names what the row
resolves to: a live `docs/design/` document or a registered identifier
family ([`194-tracking-index`](194-tracking-index.mdc)). Gated by
`scripts/ci/check_followups_owners.py`.

A PR number may be cited beside an owner. It is not an owner on its own.
PRs merge and close, and a row whose only owner is a merged PR is a
row nobody owns. Six rows once named "the E2 lane" as owner while no
such lane existed in any form; that is the shape the cell makes
visible (rule 22). Rows predating the cell are grandfathered by exact
heading in a list that only burns down.
